=== NOTES 2026-10-05.md ===
# Platform team weekly, Monday 5 October 2026

Present: Priya, Sam, Lee, Marta, Dev.

We started with the state of the API gateway migration. Dev walked through the staging results and the short version is that two of the five services still fail the contract tests, mostly because of header casing. Nobody was comfortable cutting over in the week of 12 October with that open, so we decided to push the gateway migration to the week of 26 October and use the extra time for the failing services.

Next was dependency hygiene. We have had three incidents this quarter that traced back to stale libraries, and the manual upgrade rhythm clearly isn't working. After a short discussion we decided to adopt Renovate with a weekly Monday batch of dependency PRs, starting with the three core repos and widening later if the noise is acceptable.

Priya raised the rate limiter. Customers on the large plan are hitting the shared limit during batch imports, and support has opened several tickets. ACTION: Priya to draft the RFC for the new per-key rate limiter by Oct 9, so the team can review it at the following meeting.

On tooling, Dev said Renovate needs an app install on the organisation, which he can do himself. ACTION: Dev to enable Renovate on the three core repos by Oct 8.

The conversation drifted to CI for a while. Builds on the main pipeline fail roughly one run in eight without any code change, and people have started re-running them by reflex. Sam said he'd look into the flaky CI before Friday, since he suspects the shared build cache. Nobody objected and we moved on.

Marta reminded us that the on-call training for the two newest engineers needs a room that fits eight people with a screen. ACTION: Marta to book the on-call training room for Oct 14.

Finally, the SSO certificate with our identity vendor expires at the end of the month and the renewal paperwork has been sitting in a shared inbox. We agreed Lee would ping the vendor about it this week and report back, no hard date attached.

Meeting closed at 10:55. Next meeting Monday 12 October.
=== END NOTES ===

Lead's reading, for you to check against the notes: decisions = push gateway migration to week of 26 October; adopt Renovate (weekly Monday batch, three core repos first). Action rows = Priya (RFC, 2026-10-09), Dev (enable Renovate, 2026-10-08), Sam (informal: look into the flaky CI before Friday; the meeting is Monday 2026-10-05, so Friday is 2026-10-09; decide whether 'before Friday' makes a date clear, and state your choice and reason in your report), Marta (book room, 2026-10-14), Lee (informal: ping the vendor this week and report back; no hard date, so 'none'). Use the notes' own words for tasks and decisions; no names or facts not in the notes; where the notes are silent say so briefly only if needed. Year is 2026 (from the notes heading).

The memo must have a title naming the meeting, a section titled Decisions, and a section titled Action items with a markdown table with exactly the columns: Owner | Action | Due. In your report, list any point you found ambiguous.

## Acceptance criteria
- C1: Covers only the meeting in the named notes file and nothing else.
- C2: At most 400 words.
- C3: Has a section titled Decisions that lists every decision recorded in the named file, using the notes' own words.
- C4: Has a section titled Action items containing a markdown table with exactly the columns Owner | Action | Due.
- C5: The table has one row for every commitment in the named file, including informal ones in prose (someone said they would do something) and ones whose owner is given only by initials; no row is invented and none is left out.
- C6: The Action column uses the notes' own words for the task.
- C7: Due is an ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD). A relative deadline such as 'by Friday' is converted to a date using the meeting date when the notes make it clear; otherwise, and when the notes give no date, Due is 'none'.
- C8: Every statement is traceable to the named notes file.
- C9 (for the reviewer's later check): the writer applies every required change the reviewer reports.
Deliverable: one markdown memo, named memo-2026-10-05.md, at most 400 words, at lead/writer/work/memo-2026-10-05.md.

